<section class="lp-why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
  <div class="lp-why-text">
    <h2 id="why-title">Built up in love.</h2>
    <p class="lp-why-ref">Ephesians 4:15–16</p>
    <p>Ephesians 4 describes a church as a body: joined and held together, every part doing its work, building itself up in love. A meal train is that. So is a workday, a retreat, the Tuesday someone drives a casserole across town.</p>
    <p>Most of that work doesn’t fail for lack of love. It stalls in the logistics: the spreadsheet nobody can find, the text thread that lost a name, the one person holding every detail in their head.</p>
    <p>Flockwork takes the logistics so the body can do its work. When the planning takes an evening instead of a month, a church says yes more often.</p>
  </div>
  <%= image_tag "marketing/alvarez-family.jpg", width: 1152, height: 768, loading: "lazy", alt: "A couple on a leather couch, smiling down at the newborn in their arms" %>
</section>
